[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You could have a great conversation with a pal, come back 3 days later, and the context that made it great was gone. So, we rebuild memory around the relationship itself. The profile is its understanding of who you are, preferences, goals, how you communicate,'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the people in your life, and a timeline. What\'s actually happened between you. That\'s the shift. From a system waiting for instructions to one that has enough context to know when it can help. It\'s a'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'step towards a pal that doesn\'t just answer. One that helps before you ask. And what each pal learns is shaped by its role. A tutor shouldn\'t just know which lesson you finished. It remembers how you'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'learn, where you struggle, what made you nervous last time. A coach learns what motivates you, and what tends to get in your way. Not just the goals you typed into a form. Sometimes a pal should know things about'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a person before the first conversation starts. If you already know who\'s going to be talking to it, you can give it that context ahead of time. Everything it learns along the way is visible to you. You can look at it, fix'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'what\'s wrong, or delete it. The whole idea is memory you can see and change. Every conversation should build on the last. That\'s memories.'
